  "metadata": {
    "slug": "how-your-usage-is-counted",
    "title": "How your usage is counted in Capgo",
    "description": "Understand how Capgo count your usage, and use it at best. Learn to manage better your plan",
    "author": "Martin Donadieu",
    "author_image_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4084527?v=4",
    "author_url": "https://x.com/martindonadieu",
    "created_at": "2022-11-25 00:00:00+00:00",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-27 16:41:24+00:00",
    "head_image": "/usage_explained.webp",
    "head_image_alt": "How your usage is counted in Capgo Capgo blog illustration",
    "keywords": "mobile app development, live updates, OTA updates, continuous integration, mobile app updates",
    "tag": "Solution",
    "published": true,
    "locale": "en",
    "origin": "human",
    "next_blog": ""
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 2,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 2,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "In Capgo, 3 values are counted and important to understand"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "location": {
        "line": 3,
        "column": 1
      },
      "ordered": false,
      "start": null,
      "spread": false,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "location": {
            "line": 3,
            "column": 1
          },
          "spread": false,
          "checked": null,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "location": {
                "line": 3,
                "column": 3
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "location": {
                    "line": 3,
                    "column": 3
                  },
                  "text": "User's"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "location": {
            "line": 4,
            "column": 1
          },
          "spread": false,
          "checked": null,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "location": {
                "line": 4,
                "column": 3
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "location": {
                    "line": 4,
                    "column": 3
                  },
                  "text": "Storage"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "location": {
            "line": 5,
            "column": 1
          },
          "spread": false,
          "checked": null,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "location": {
                "line": 5,
                "column": 3
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "location": {
                    "line": 5,
                    "column": 3
                  },
                  "text": "Bandwidth"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 7,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 7,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "Each one as a slight different way of being counted"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "location": {
        "line": 10,
        "column": 1
      },
      "depth": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 10,
            "column": 4
          },
          "text": "Users"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 12,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 12,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "Each time a user download your Capacitor JS app and opens it, it will send a request to Capgo backend to know is update is available.\nWhen the app does that, it sends little information, including the most important one "
        },
        {
          "type": "inlineCode",
          "location": {
            "line": 13,
            "column": 87
          },
          "text": "DeviceID"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 15,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "inlineCode",
          "location": {
            "line": 15,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "DeviceID"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 15,
            "column": 11
          },
          "text": ": is a unique ID (UUID) generated on the device. "
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "location": {
            "line": 15,
            "column": 60
          },
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "location": {
                "line": 15,
                "column": 62
              },
              "text": "Starting from plugin version v5.10.0, v6.25.0 and v7.25.0"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 15,
            "column": 121
          },
          "text": ", this ID now persists across app reinstalls (stored securely in device storage). Prior to these versions, the ID was reset with each app installation."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 17,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 17,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "Each time your account receives a new Device ID, it saved in database.\nEach time an old "
        },
        {
          "type": "inlineCode",
          "location": {
            "line": 18,
            "column": 18
          },
          "text": "DeviceID"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 18,
            "column": 28
          },
          "text": " request an update (app open), it got is record updated (updated_at in the database)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 20,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 20,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "This data is saved in 2 places:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "location": {
        "line": 21,
        "column": 1
      },
      "ordered": false,
      "start": null,
      "spread": false,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "location": {
            "line": 21,
            "column": 1
          },
          "spread": false,
          "checked": null,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "location": {
                "line": 21,
                "column": 3
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "location": {
                    "line": 21,
                    "column": 3
                  },
                  "text": "device table with "
                },
                {
                  "type": "inlineCode",
                  "location": {
                    "line": 21,
                    "column": 21
                  },
                  "text": "update_at"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "location": {
                    "line": 21,
                    "column": 32
                  },
                  "text": " value"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "location": {
            "line": 22,
            "column": 1
          },
          "spread": false,
          "checked": null,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "location": {
                "line": 22,
                "column": 3
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "location": {
                    "line": 22,
                    "column": 3
                  },
                  "text": "app_stats with daily counter who represents the number of device who became active today and haven't been active this month."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 24,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 24,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "For plan limit the first method is used because it's 100% reliable, for displaying the chart the second one is used.\nYou can see both in your account on the home page:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "location": {
        "line": 26,
        "column": 1
      },
      "ordered": false,
      "start": null,
      "spread": false,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "location": {
            "line": 26,
            "column": 1
          },
          "spread": false,
          "checked": null,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "location": {
                "line": 26,
                "column": 3
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "location": {
                    "line": 26,
                    "column": 3
                  },
                  "text": "in the chart is the second method"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "location": {
            "line": 27,
            "column": 1
          },
          "spread": false,
          "checked": null,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "location": {
                "line": 27,
                "column": 3
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "location": {
                    "line": 27,
                    "column": 3
                  },
                  "text": "in the table of apps is the first method."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "blockquote",
      "location": {
        "line": 29,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "location": {
            "line": 29,
            "column": 3
          },
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "location": {
                "line": 29,
                "column": 3
              },
              "text": "Capgo don't count emulator and dev build in your usage. Keep in mind after the trial you can't have more than 3% of them, or that will lock your account, until you fix it."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "blockquote",
      "location": {
        "line": 31,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "location": {
            "line": 31,
            "column": 3
          },
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "location": {
                "line": 31,
                "column": 3
              },
              "text": "Capgo is also doing some filtering for you. If you have CI/CD configured to send your version to Google PLAY, Google is running your Capacitor app each time to 20+ real device. During the 4 first hours of a new bundle, we block Google data center IP to prevent them to being counted."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 33,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 33,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "Each month, this data starts from zero."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "location": {
        "line": 36,
        "column": 1
      },
      "ordered": false,
      "start": null,
      "spread": false,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "location": {
            "line": 36,
            "column": 1
          },
          "spread": false,
          "checked": null,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "location": {
                "line": 36,
                "column": 3
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "location": {
                    "line": 36,
                    "column": 3
                  },
                  "text": "Create or update a device in my database at each device request"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "location": {
            "line": 37,
            "column": 1
          },
          "spread": false,
          "checked": null,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "location": {
                "line": 37,
                "column": 3
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "location": {
                    "line": 37,
                    "column": 3
                  },
                  "text": "Add to a daily counter the number of active device who hasn't been active this month."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 39,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 39,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "The first method returns: 900+ users\nwhile the second one is at 200+ users on your account\nFor plan limit I use the first method, who is 100% reliable, and to display the chart I use the second one.\nYou can see both on your account home page."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "location": {
        "line": 44,
        "column": 1
      },
      "depth": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 44,
            "column": 4
          },
          "text": "Storage"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 46,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 46,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "Each time you upload a bundle, this number is increased by the size of the upload."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 48,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 48,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "This data is only related to your upload size, the better your app size is, the better you stay in your plan."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 50,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 50,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "If you reach the limit or near, you can list your bundles with the CLI:\n"
        },
        {
          "type": "inlineCode",
          "location": {
            "line": 51,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "npx @capgo/cli@latest bundle list"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 51,
            "column": 36
          },
          "text": "\nTo see what you could clean, removing a bundle, free the storage but don't delete the stats."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 54,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 54,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "When you are ready for cleanup, use this command to remove many bundles:\n"
        },
        {
          "type": "inlineCode",
          "location": {
            "line": 55,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "npx @capgo/cli@latest bundle cleanup"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 57,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 57,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "PS: this is good for the planet, but also for your wallet 💪."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "blockquote",
      "location": {
        "line": 59,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "location": {
            "line": 59,
            "column": 3
          },
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "location": {
                "line": 59,
                "column": 3
              },
              "text": "You can also use the "
            },
            {
              "type": "inlineCode",
              "location": {
                "line": 59,
                "column": 24
              },
              "text": "--external"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "location": {
                "line": 59,
                "column": 36
              },
              "text": " of upload to use your storage, and not count in your plan."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "location": {
        "line": 61,
        "column": 1
      },
      "depth": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 61,
            "column": 4
          },
          "text": "Bandwidth"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 63,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 63,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "The calculation of this value is a bit more complex, but the idea is the same as the storage."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 65,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 65,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "Each time a user download a bundle, this number is increased by the size of the download."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 67,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 67,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "This data is only related to your download size, the better your Capacitor JS app size is, the better you stay in your plan."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "blockquote",
      "location": {
        "line": 69,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "location": {
            "line": 69,
            "column": 3
          },
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "location": {
                "line": 69,
                "column": 3
              },
              "text": "One important thing to note, Capgo cannot see what size is downloaded, it only sees the size of the bundle. So if you have a big bundle, and you have many users who fail to download it, you will reach the limit quickly."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 71,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 71,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "The best way to stay in your plan is to have a small bundle, and if you can't, show a download bar to your user, and let them know how much they have left to download."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 73,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 73,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "In the future, Capgo will improve the download system to have more chances to download the bundle at one time."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "location": {
        "line": 75,
        "column": 1
      },
      "depth": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 75,
            "column": 4
          },
          "text": "Keep going from How your usage is counted in Capgo"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 77,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 77,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "If you are using "
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "location": {
            "line": 77,
            "column": 18
          },
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "location": {
                "line": 77,
                "column": 20
              },
              "text": "How your usage is counted in Capgo"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 77,
            "column": 56
          },
          "text": " to plan live update delivery, connect it with "
        },
